{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"A change in control of an ETF’s principal adviser generally causes an **assignment** of its advisory contract, which automatically terminates the contract under the Investment Company Act. The ETF cannot simply continue under the old agreement.\n\nThe replacement principal advisory contract must be approved by the fund’s board, including a majority of its independent directors, and by the ETF’s shareholders. Shareholder approval generally means a majority of the outstanding voting securities under the Act. The board must also evaluate the contract and related materials under its fiduciary duties and applicable disclosure requirements.\n\nA narrow exception may apply to certain reorganizations that do not result in a change of actual control or management; whether a transaction triggers assignment depends on its facts and the contract’s terms."}}
